{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Google-Analytics","title":"Sending to Google Analytics"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") for a Google Analytics 4 stream in one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"call. It checks the measurement ID and the API secret, and posts to the Measurement Protocol’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\/mp\/collect","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint of the region ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". It splits each batch to the Measurement Protocol’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"): 25 events and 100 KB a request. A batch with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. The destination retries no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own. An app doesn’t use it:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its events reach Google Analytics through TraffluentCollector (Getting an app’s events to Google"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Analytics, below)."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The API secret stays on a server","level":3,"anchor":"The-API-secret-stays-on-a-server"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol takes only requests that carry one of the stream’s API secrets, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anyone holding that secret can send events to the property. Google’s docs say not to expose it in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an app, and an app’s binary can be read by anyone who installs it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So the whole module is compiled for macOS and Linux alone, where a server runs. An app for iOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iPadOS, tvOS, watchOS, visionOS or Mac Catalyst that calls the factory, or names the encoder, fails","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to compile. A Mac app, AppKit or SwiftUI, compiles the factory as a Mac server does, but the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factory refuses it at run time: it throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError\/appBundle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"process’s main bundle is an ","type":"text"},{"code":".app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"code":".appex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Nothing stops a Mac app from building an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with this encoder and an endpoint it writes itself, secret and all, so don’t.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The secret is also in the query of every request’s URL. Don’t log the destination, its requests or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a transport’s URLs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for an empty measurement ID, for one that isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G-"},{"text":" followed by uppercase letters and digits, and for an empty API secret. The region has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".global"},{"text":" is Google’s default endpoint, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".eu"},{"text":" has Google collect the data in the EU.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Getting an app’s events to Google Analytics","level":3,"anchor":"Getting-an-apps-events-to-Google-Analytics"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app’s events reach Google Analytics through TraffluentCollector, which forwards the records it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepts to a Google Analytics 4 web stream over the Measurement Protocol. The app holds no Google"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"secret and doesn’t link this module. It sends to the collector as any source does: an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":") and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collector’s API key. Its tracker’s sessions enricher gives each record the session that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collector sends as its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":". In the app, in Swift:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import TrackingPlans","import Traffluent","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com\/v1\/batches","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(apiKey)\"],  \/\/ the collector's API key, not Google's","    encoder: CollectorBatchEncoder(plan: plan))","\/\/ The sessions enricher gives each record the session the collector sends as its client_id.","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The measurement ID, the API secret and the region are set in the collector’s environment, not in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Swift and not in the app:"}]},{"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing","code":["SERVER_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-ABC123                 # the web stream's measurement ID","SERVER_GA4_API_SECRET=replace-with-the-api-secret  # one of that stream's Measurement Protocol API secrets","SERVER_GA4_REGION=global                           # or eu; global when unset","SERVER_TRACKING_PLAN=\/srv\/tracking-plan            # the exported plan, required to forward"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set the measurement ID and the API secret together; with neither set, nothing is forwarded. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"variable set empty counts as unset. The collector refuses to start, in development as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"production, when only some are set, when the region is neither ","type":"text"},{"code":"global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" nor ","type":"text"},{"code":"eu","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or when it has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no tracking plan, which it needs because the plan marks which properties are sensitive. Its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"GET \/v1\/admin\/forwarding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" route, and the Forwarding screens of its web UI and iOS app, report the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measurement ID and the region, how many records are pending, forwarded and skipped, and the last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"failure. No route answers the API secret.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector writes the same Measurement Protocol requests as this module’s encoder: one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client’s events a request, at most 25 events and 100,000 bytes. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session as two decimal halves, or the record’s identifier when it has no session. Each event has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" from a version 7 session’s start and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp_micros"},{"type":"text","text":", and ad consent is denied."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Its parameters are the properties with every property the plan marks sensitive left out, objects"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and arrays flattened into names joined by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":", and nulls left out. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", user properties,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"location or device is sent, and no other context value. It skips the same records this module’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder does (reserved or malformed names, more than 25 parameters, a string over 100 bytes), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a record more than 72 hours older or 15 minutes newer than the moment the collector encodes it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The collector logs each skipped record and counts it in the status. The app’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":" don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hear of it, since the collector accepted the record."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only records the plan accepted, and that the collector stored for the first time, are queued to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forward, in the same statement that stores them. So a rejected record is never forwarded, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither are the records of a batch the app sends again, which the collector holds already. Records it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stored while forwarding wasn’t configured aren’t forwarded later. A service drains the queue: it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"claims up to 100 records for 60 seconds, so collectors sharing a database never send one record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at the same time, posts them, and settles the ones Google Analytics took. A record whose post"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"failed, or whose collector stopped, is sent again once its claim lapses, so one Google stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before the answer was lost is counted twice. The Measurement Protocol answers 2xx with a wrong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measurement ID or API secret too, so a record sent counts as forwarded whatever Google made of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it: check the property’s Realtime report after setting the variables."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Sending from a server of your own","level":3,"anchor":"Sending-from-a-server-of-your-own"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send from a server of yours instead, such as a relay in front of Google Analytics, make this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination there and hand it the records. Traffluent has no decoder that turns a collector batch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"back into records, so a relay’s job is:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read each event the app sent (its name, version, identifier, timestamp, properties and session)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decode it into the same "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type the app tracked, from a module the app and the server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"share."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Remake its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord(id:event:timestamp:sourceLocation:context:)"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app’s identifier and timestamp, and a context whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":" is the app’s session."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hand each batch of records to the destination’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"receive(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t track the events again through a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":".sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the server. That tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would give every event the server’s own session, so every user of the app would arrive in Google","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Analytics as one ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A server that tracks its own events, rather than an app’s, uses a tracker as any app does:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let googleAnalytics = try HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(","    measurementID: measurementID,  \/\/ the web or data stream's, G-…","    apiSecret: apiSecret,  \/\/ from the server's configuration, never an app's","    region: .global,  \/\/ or .eu, to have Google collect the data in the EU","    plan: plan)","\/\/ A server tracking its own events: its sessions are the server's.","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: googleAnalytics)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rest of this article describes this module’s destination."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What Google Analytics receives","level":3,"anchor":"What-Google-Analytics-receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request holds one client’s events, as the Measurement Protocol takes one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, from the sessions enricher, written as the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"halves of its UUID in decimal, joined by a period, the form the Measurement Protocol asks for. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, in a request of its own. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter is the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, so Google Analytics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"groups the session’s events, and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp_micros"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s timestamp. Every request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sends ad consent as denied, so Google uses none of the events for advertising."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", user properties, location, IP address, device or user agent is sent, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"advertising identifier. The record’s vendor identifier, trace context and standard context aren’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent either. Google Analytics counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports, and so is each record sent without a session."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"engagement_time_msec"},{"text":" is sent, as Traffluent doesn’t measure engagement. Without it the events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"don’t count toward engagement time or engaged sessions, and the Realtime and Users reports can show","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no users while events arrive. Check the event counts, not the user counts, to see that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination works.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and become the event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"params","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Google Analytics takes only strings, numbers and booleans, so a nested value is spread into a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameter for each value it holds, named after its path joined by ","type":"text"},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"cart_size","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tags_0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left out.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Records sent twice","level":3,"anchor":"Records-sent-twice"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol has no field that identifies an event, so Google Analytics can’t tell a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"repeat from a new event, and counts every one it receives. A record is sent more than once when a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request is retried after Google stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancelled batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each such record is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counted twice in Google Analytics."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Records left out","level":3,"anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name, or a parameter’s name, is longer than 40 bytes, doesn’t start with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"letter, or holds anything but letters, numbers and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name Google Analytics keeps (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_start"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"first_visit"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"text":" and the rest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its reserved names), or takes only from an app stream (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_view"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ad_impression"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in_app_purchase"},{"text":");","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a parameter Google Analytics keeps (a ","type":"text"},{"code":"firebase_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ga_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"google_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" prefix) or named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which the encoder writes;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one of more than 25 parameters, counting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", or with a string longer than 100 bytes;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one tracked more than 71 hours before the batch is encoded, or more than 15 minutes after it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and one whose timestamp has no microseconds form;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one too large for a request.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Google Analytics wouldn’t refuse such an event: it answers 2xx either way. Under its default,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relaxed validation it stores the event without the parameter that breaks a rule, or under a name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it never checked, so the report would hold an event other than the one tracked. The encoder leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the record out and reports it instead. A Google Analytics 360 property takes values of up to 500"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"characters, but the encoder holds every property to the standard 100 bytes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError"},{"text":". The encoder logs a notice for each event and property of the plan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"named as Google Analytics refuses when the destination is made; rename such an event or property,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"raising the event’s version, to send it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What the Measurement Protocol doesn’t report","level":3,"anchor":"What-the-Measurement-Protocol-doesnt-report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol answers 2xx to every request it receives, including one it can’t read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose events it doesn’t store. A wrong measurement ID or API secret is answered 2xx with nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stored, so check the property’s Realtime event counts after setting the destination up. Google’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validation server, ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/debug\/mp\/collect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", checks a body’s shape but not the measurement ID or the API","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"secret, so a body it accepts can still be stored nowhere. A record older than 72 hours is stored as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"if it happened 72 hours ago, so the encoder leaves out one older than 71 hours, the hour to spare","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the request to reach Google and clocks that disagree. A request is encoded once and retried as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it is, so the encoder gives each request a deadline 71 hours after its oldest record was tracked. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request still failing by then isn’t sent again: the destination drops the whole request, its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"younger records too, and reports it on ","type":"text"},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with every one of its records’ identifiers.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude, Mixpanel or Segment, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Google Analytics receives, and why, in more detail."}]}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","role":"collection","externalID":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","modules":[{"name":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsRegion":{"title":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where Google Analytics collects a stream’s events, which decides the Measurement Protocol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"endpoint they are posted to."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsregion","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion"}]},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","abstract":[{"text":"A destination on a server that sends batches to the Google Analytics web or data stream of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"measurementID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", authenticated by its ","type":"text"},{"code":"apiSecret","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", through ","type":"text"},{"code":"transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", retrying a send that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails for now with the waits of ","type":"text"},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoi